  Parking inside **Hudson Tea Garage** is your safest bet tonight—**Union City enforces a city-wide overnight permit rule**, so leaving a rental car on Palisade Ave overnight risks a \$60 ticket.

  ### Overnight parking: Palisade Ave (Union City) vs. Hudson Tea Garage

  * **Palisade Ave, Union City (Risky without a permit):** Per the [Union City Parking Authority](https://www.ucpanj.org/_Content/pdf/Permit-Price-Changes-as-of-9-1-2024-Flyer.pdf), a **residential or visitor permit is required city-wide from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM** (violations carry a **\$60** fine per the [UCPA Violations Schedule](https://www.ucpanj.org/Permits)). Unless you have a Union City visitor permit hangtag, don't park on Palisade Ave overnight—even though daytime meters aren't enforced on Sundays.
  * **Hudson Tea Garage — <EntityLink entity_type="place" entity_id="ChIJv0py_tZZwokRD4YHdNuts1c">LAZ Parking Hudson Tea Parking Facility</EntityLink> (Safest):** Located right at **1450 Bloomfield St** (`+1 201-795-5285`), the public garage is **open 24/7** and puts the car in the same building as the Avis counter for your 8:00 AM drop-off.
    * **Where to park:** Pull a regular ticket at the gate or book ahead on [SpotHero](https://spothero.com/facility/17084/1450-bloomfield-st-2-parking) (often around **\$12** depending on hours; scan the QR code instead of pulling a ticket if using SpotHero).
    * **What to avoid:** Park **only in non-reserved spaces**—do **not** park in spots marked **"Reserved"** or **"AVIS Parking Only"** ([SpotHero Facility Rules](https://spothero.com/facility/17084/1450-bloomfield-st-2-parking)), as leaving an unreturned car in an Avis-only bay overnight doesn't close your contract and risks towing.

  ### Waiving extra-day fees for traffic and app errors

  Avis's standard policy charges hourly late fees (three-fourths of the daily rate plus \$0.01 per hour on daily/weekend rates) up to an extra day once you pass your 24-hour window, plus up to **\$15/day** if you don't call **1-800-230-4898** to extend ([Avis Reservations FAQ](https://www.avis.com/en/customer-service/faqs/usa/reservations); [Avis Rental Car Return FAQ](https://www.avis.com/en/help/usa-faqs/rental-car-return)). Because 1450 Bloomfield has no drop box, here is how to maximize your chances of getting the extra charges waived as a **President's Club** member:

  1. **Screenshot the app error now:** Capture the error screen (with the timestamp visible) and your call log if you tried reaching the desk.
  2. **Call President's Club / 1-800-230-4898 tonight:** Have the agent add a timestamped note to your agreement stating that traffic delayed your return, the Avis app errored out when you tried to extend, and the Hoboken branch has no after-hours drop box. That note protects you from the unnotified-late penalty and backs up your waiver request.
  3. **Ask the Hoboken counter manager at 8:00 AM:** Politely explain the traffic delay, show the app error screenshot, and ask if they can close out the contract at the original return time (or waive the extra-day charge) as a **President's Club courtesy**.
  4. **Escalate post-rental if needed:** If the local desk system won't let them override the extra day, call **Avis Customer Service at 1-800-352-7900** (or your dedicated President's Club line in the app) once the final receipt posts. Having the night-before call note plus app screenshots gives them clear grounds to issue a credit.

  <FollowUp label="Want a short script for what to say to the Avis agent tonight?" query="Give me a short script for what to tell the Avis President's Club agent tonight and the Hoboken desk manager tomorrow morning to get the extra-day fee waived." />

